          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Check Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771626598794"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_CHECK_INTENT",
          "id": "1766726660548",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766726660551_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role: You are a strict decision engine. You must only use the provided inputs: chat history, use_message, offer_preview.\n\nInputs\n* chat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n* user_message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n* offer_preview: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.offerDetails}} \n\nTask\n1. Determine if the user has confirmed deletion of the same offer preview that appears in offer_preview. offer_preview might be empty. In that case set \"previewConfirm\" to \"No\", \"deleteConfirmed\" to \"No\"\n2. Ensure the user is not asking to modify the offer preview, not switching to a different topic, and not asking to delete a different offer.\n3. Determine whether the user is cancelling/rejecting/not proceeding with the deletion preview. If so, set updatePreviewWithDetails to \"No\".\n4. Determine whether the user wants to modify the preview. If the user wants modifications AND provides additional concrete details/instructions to apply, set updatePreviewWithDetails to \"Yes\".\n5. If the user wants to modify the preview but does NOT provide any additional concrete details/instructions (i.e., they just say “change it”, “edit it”, “update it”, etc. without specifics), set updatePreviewWithDetails to \"No\".\n6. Output updatePreviewWithDetails as \"Yes\" or \"No\" based only on whether the user is requesting modifications with sufficient additional details (NOT based on deletion confirmation).\n\nStrict Definitions / Rules\nA) Deletion Confirmation (deleteConfirmed)\nSet deleteConfirmed to \"Yes\" only if all are true:\n* The user uses clear, explicit confirmation language (e.g., “yes delete it”, “confirm delete”, “go ahead and delete”, “delete this offer”, “I confirm”).\n* The confirmation clearly refers to the offer in offer_preview (by direct reference like “this offer”, “the above”, or by matching identifiers/details). offer_preview is not empty!\n* The user is not expressing hesitation, conditions, or alternatives.\n* The user is not requesting modifications.\n*Treat “Confirm …” / “Please confirm …” / “Confirm discarding …” phrasing as an explicit confirmation command (deleteConfirmed = \"Yes\") when it is instructing the system to proceed with deletion of the currently shown preview, NOT when it is a question asking for information.\n* The confirmation might contain details of the offer and it is still a valid confirmation. For example: “Please confirm discarding (permanently deleting) all draft offers for business unit Vision Operations in currency USD where the unpaid amount is greater than 20,000 USD.” -> deleteConfirmed is set to 'Yes'\n*IMPORTANT: draft offers are short listed draft offers. The two terms are used interchangeable. \nSet deleteConfirmed to \"No\" if:\n* offer_preview is empty/null\n* The user is unsure (“maybe”, “not sure”, “let’s wait”).\n* The user asks questions instead of confirming (“what happens if…”, “can I undo…”).\n* The user introduces conditions (“delete it if…”, “only if…”).\n* The user requests changes (“edit/modify/update the offer first”).\n* The user wants a different action or a different offer.\n* The user says “no”, “don’t delete”, “cancel”.\n\nB) Update Intent With Details (updatePreviewWithDetails) Purpose: Detect whether the user wants to modify the shown preview AND the latest user_message contains NEW actionable details beyond the chat history.\n\nGlobal “No” overrides — set updatePreviewWithDetails = \"No\" if any are true:\n1. The user rejects/cancels/not proceeding with the preview or deletion flow (e.g., “no”, “don’t delete”, “cancel”, “stop”, “never mind”, “not this offer”).\n2. The user confirms deletion (they are proceeding to delete rather than modify).\n3. The user is switching topics or requesting a different action unrelated to modifying the shown offer.\n4. The user’s intent is ambiguous/unclear.\n5. The user asks to modify but provides no concrete details (e.g., “change it”, “edit it”, “update it”, “revise it” with no specifics).\n6. The user provides details, but they are NOT new vs chat history (they are repeats, confirmations, or paraphrases without adding actionable delta).\n\nSet updatePreviewWithDetails = \"Yes\" only if all are true:\n1. The user is requesting modifications to the shown offer preview (not a different offer).\n2. The latest user_message provides at least one concrete, actionable change/detail to apply.\n3. HISTORY DELTA REQUIREMENT: At least one of those actionable details is NEW compared to what the user has already specified anywhere in chat history.\n\nHistory Delta Rules (must follow)\n1. Extract prior user-provided modification instructions from chat history:\n    * Look for any earlier user messages that requested edits or provided specifics (fields, values, replacements, additions/removals, constraints).\n2. Normalize instructions for comparison:\n    * Treat “payment terms to Net 30” and “set payment to net30” as the same instruction.\n3. Determine if user_message contains any NEW actionable instruction or new conditions not already present: NEW actionable details include (examples):\n    * New field/attribute to change (e.g., add “delivery date”, “supplier address”, “discount rate”, “supplier names”).\n    * New value/number/date/identifier (e.g., change amount to $50K; change end date to 6/30).\n    * New constraint/condition for the edit (e.g., “keep the title the same but shorten the summary to 2 lines”).\n    * Clarification that resolves ambiguity (e.g., previously “update term” now “update payment term to Net 45”).\n4. NOT new (set to \"No\" if these are the only things present):\n    * Pure acknowledgments: “yes”, “ok”, “sounds good”, “do that”, “apply those changes”.\n    * Repeating the same details already in history with no additions.\n    * Vague edit requests with no specifics.\n5. Key Upgrade (important)\nUsers often phrase preview modifications using “delete” language (e.g., “Delete only X”, “Delete just supplier Y”). Treat these as modification requests (updatePreviewWithDetails = \"Yes\") when they change the scope/filters of what would be deleted, NOT as deletion confirmation.\n\nOutput Format (JSON only) Return only valid JSON, no extra text: { \"deleteConfirmed\": \"Yes|No\", \"updatePreviewWithDetails\": \"Yes|No\", \"reason\": \"brief explanation referencing user intent + whether it matches the preview\" }\n\nExample Decisions (internal guidance)\n* User: “Yes, delete it.” + preview exists → deleteConfirmed: Yes, updatePreviewWithDetails: No\n* User: “Cancel—don’t proceed.” → deleteConfirmed: No, updatePreviewWithDetails: No\n* User: “Change the payment terms to XYZ.” → deleteConfirmed: No, updatePreviewWithDetails: Yes\n* User: “Edit the offer.” (no specifics) → deleteConfirmed: No, updatePreviewWithDetails: No\n* User: “Delete offer ABC123” but preview is XYZ999 → deleteConfirmed: No, updatePreviewWithDetails: No\n* User: “That’s not the right offer.” → deleteConfirmed: No, updatePreviewWithDetails: No"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"deleteConfirmed\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"updatePreviewWithDetails\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Variables for Initiatialization"
          },
          "outcomes": {
