        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Offer Payload Constructor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771020029603"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_OFFER_PAYLOAD_CONSTRUCTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769804979324",
          "id": "1769543312259",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769543312260_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the Offer Delete Filter Builder.\nYour task is to construct:\n1) additionalFilter (a single SQL-like predicate string)\n2) eligibleFilter (\"Yes\" / \"No\")\nbased on the current user input and the full conversation history.\n\nThe user wants to discard/delete draft offers, so your job is to identify the filters the user wants to apply to select which draft offers to delete.\n\n**Core Responsibility**\nYou must extract, retain, and reapply all valid filter criteria explicitly mentioned across:\n* Current User Input\n* Full Session History\n* Suppliers-to-delete input list (this determines whether suppliers are a filter)\n\nIf the current user input is a follow-up, you must merge it with previously stated filters unless the user explicitly removes/changes them. Do not drop previously applied filters due to partial follow-ups.\n\nInputs:\n* Current User Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n* Session History: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n* Suppliers they want to delete (this indicates supplier filtering): {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.suppliers}}\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nA) Accepted (Eligible) Filter Requests (for eligibleFilter)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nThe following user filter requests are considered ACCEPTED and must NOT cause eligibleFilter=\"No\":\n1. Program Type\n2. Currency\n3. Email presence/absence\n4. Suppliers (ONLY if supplier filtering is indicated by the suppliers-to-delete list; do not infer from chat)\n5. Unpaid amount\n6. Business Unit\n\neligibleFilter rules:\n* eligibleFilter = \"Yes\" if ALL filter requests found in the current input + history are within the Accepted list above (and supplier filtering rules).\n* eligibleFilter = \"No\" if the user requests at least one filter attribute outside the Accepted list anywhere in the conversation.\n  Examples of NOT accepted (eligibleFilter=\"No\"):\n  * dates/time windows (e.g., “last week”, “before Jan 1”)\n  * country, payment terms, legal entity, etc. (unless listed as Accepted above)\n\nImportant: Currency and Business Unit are ACCEPTED requests. They must NOT make eligibleFilter=\"No\".\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nB) Filters to Actually Build into additionalFilter (Supported for Construction)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nYou must ONLY construct additionalFilter using these attributes (and ONLY these):\n1. Program Type → financingOptionTypeCode\n2. Email condition → emailAddress (null / not null)\n3. Suppliers → supplierName (ONLY if suppliers-to-delete list is present and non-empty)\n4. Unpaid amount → totalUnpaidAmount\n\nSpecial rule (NO-OP in additionalFilter):\n* Currency and Business Unit may be requested by the user, and are ACCEPTED for eligibility,\n  but you MUST NOT add them to additionalFilter.\n  (Assume Currency and Business Unit are handled by another layer/system.)\n\nIgnore all other attributes.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nC) Special Handling: “Short listed draft” / “Shortlisted drafts”\n------------------------------------------------------------\n* Do NOT apply “short listed/shortlisted” as a filter in additionalFilter.\n* Treat it as a no-op qualifier.\n* Do NOT mark it as unsupported.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nD) Supplier Filter Rule (Important)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n* If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.suppliers}} is present and non-empty, then suppliers ARE a filter and you MUST filter by supplierName using all name values from that list.\n  * If one supplier: supplierName = 'Supplier A'\n  * If multiple: supplierName IN ('Supplier A','Supplier B')\n* If that suppliers list is missing or empty:\n  * Do not apply supplierName filters\nDo not infer suppliers from chat history.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nE) Filter Persistence & Precedence Rules\n------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Filter Accumulation (Cumulative Across Turns)\n* Treat filters as cumulative across turns.\n* If an accepted/supported filter was explicitly stated earlier and not contradicted later, it must be retained.\n\n2. Override Behavior\n* If the user re-specifies an accepted/supported filter, the latest value wins.\n* If the user explicitly removes a filter (e.g., “all program types”, “regardless of email”), then remove that filter.\n\n3. Partial Follow-ups\n* If the user mentions only one attribute in the latest turn, merge it with all existing retained filters from history.\n\n4. No Assumptions\n* Include only filters explicitly stated in current input/history, plus supplier filtering if indicated by the suppliers-to-delete list.\n* Do not guess values.\n\n5. No Filter Found (for additionalFilter construction)\n* If none of the construction-supported filters are found, return:\n  additionalFilter: \"1=1\"\n\nSemantic meaning:\n* “Delete offers with email missing” → emailAddress = null (select those offers to delete)\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nF) Supported Filter Mappings (for additionalFilter construction)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nProgram Type → financingOptionTypeCode\n* Dynamic Discounting → 'DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING'\n* Virtual Card → 'VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD'\n* Supply Chain Financing → 'SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING'\n\nEmail condition → emailAddress\n* “email missing / no email / blank email / null email” → emailAddress = null\n* “has email / email present / not null email” → emailAddress != null\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nG) Filter Construction Rules\n------------------------------------------------------------\n* Build one single valid filter string.\n* Combine multiple conditions using: AND\n* Do not include unsupported-for-construction attributes (including Currency and Business Unit).\n* Do not omit previously identified construction-supported filters (unless removed/overridden).\n* If no construction-supported filter is found, use \"1=1\".\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nH) Output Requirements\n------------------------------------------------------------\nReturn only the JSON below (no explanation, no extra text):\n{\n  \"additionalFilter\": \"<constructed filter>\",\n  \"eligibleFilter\": \"Yes\" | \"No\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"additionalFilter\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }, \n\"eligibleFilter\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"additionalFilter\", \"eligibleFilter\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Eligible Filter Check"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "Yes": "1769543461594",
            "No": "1771020612064"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_SWITCH_ELIGIBLE_FILTER_CHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1771020029603",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771020029606_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_OFFER_PAYLOAD_CONSTRUCTOR.$output.eligibleFilter}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_FIN_PAYABLES_RETRIEVEOFFERSFORDELETION",
            "functionName": "retrieveOffersForDeletion",
            "name": "Get Offers"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769543533780"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_BO_GET_OFFERS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771020108189",
          "id": "1769543461594",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770109808680_1",
              "name": "businessUnitId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnitId}}"
